# Test fixtures are compared (and in inputio's case, byte-counted) exactly
# as checked in. Windows' git defaults to converting LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which would silently change those bytes -- inputio.in is 107 bytes on any
# Unix checkout and 109 after that conversion, which is exactly what broke
# the "STDIN agrees with READ" check under CI's first real Windows run.
Tests/*.in  -text
Tests/*.ans -text
Tests/*.dat -text
